1510	/// Check if we're at a block-level construct that can interrupt a paragraph.
1511	///
1512	/// Per CommonMark, these constructs can interrupt paragraphs:
1513	/// - ATX headings (# followed by space or EOL)
1514	/// - Fenced code blocks (``` or ~~~)
1515	/// - Block quotes (>)
1516	/// - Thematic breaks (---, ***, ___)
1517	/// - List items (-, *, +, or ordered markers) - with restrictions
1518	/// - HTML blocks (certain types)
1519	///
1520	/// Note: Setext headings and indented code blocks do NOT interrupt paragraphs.
1521	/// Also, lines with 4+ spaces of indentation cannot start these constructs
1522	/// (they would be indented code blocks instead).
1523	///
1524	/// ## List Interruption Rules (CommonMark §5.2)
